IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `csa-formula`

-- Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989 (Cth) -- a parent with relevant dependent children (a new family's children), and the
-- adjusted taxable income the Registrar may determine from an older tax year, computed from the formulas in
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03872.formulas.md, beside csa-formula.l4 (unchanged, which takes no relevant dependent
-- child into account).
--
-- Formulas used:
--   * s 41(2) (transcribed 2026-10-21, not used until now): child support income = Parent's adjusted taxable income for the
--     particular child for the day - Parent's self-support amount for the day - Parent's relevant dependent child amount for
--     the day; (5) nil if negative;
--   * s 46 Step 5 (recovered 2026-10-24): Parent's cost percentage for the child under step 3 x Costs of the child under step 4,
--     summed over the relevant dependent children, with Steps 1-4 from the text: the costs of the child are worked out under ss
--     55G and 55H on the parent's adjusted taxable income less the self-support amount, for all the relevant dependent
--     children;
--   * s 58AA(1) (recovered 2026-10-24): ATI indexation factor = AWE amount for the December quarter of the last relevant year of
--     income / AWE amount for the December quarter of the tax return year; (2) "to 3 decimal places (rounding up if the fourth
--     decimal place is 5 or more)"; used by s 58(3) and (4).
-- With those, Formula 1 (s 35) is worked again with each parent's child support income reduced by that parent's relevant
-- dependent child amount; the low income and minimum rate rules of csa-formula.l4 are applied in the same order.
--
-- SCOPE: one child support case (Formula 1), as csa-formula.l4; one percentage of care for all of a parent's relevant
-- dependent children. Multiple cases (ss 41(3), (4), 47, 55E, 55HA, 66(6); Formulas 3-6) are not encoded. The AWE amounts
-- are published by the Australian Statistician: inputs. Whether the Registrar makes a s 58 determination is the Registrar's
-- choice ("may"): the question answers what the determination would be.
--
-- SEAT: the parent assessed, as in csa-formula.l4. Edition: as csa-formula.l4 (C2026C00269). BASELINE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989 -- relevant dependent children and older tax years`

§§ `s 46 -- my relevant dependent child amount`

-- s 46 Step 1: "the difference between the parent's adjusted taxable income for the child for the day and the parent's
-- self-support amount"; Steps 2-3: the parent's percentage of care and cost percentage for the child (s 55C); Step 4: the costs
-- of the child under ss 55G and 55H, on the Step 1 amount, "as if ... references in sections 55G and 55H to children in the
-- child support case that relates to the child were references to all of the parent's relevant dependent children"; Step 5
-- (formula): cost percentage x costs of the child; the amount is "the total of the amounts worked out for each relevant
-- dependent child". A negative Step 1 amount is read as nil (no costs on no income).
@export What is my relevant dependent child amount, for the children of my new household (s 46)?
GIVEN `my adjusted taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your adjusted taxable income (s 43)
      `the annualised MTAWE figure` IS A NUMBER @desc The annualised MTAWE figure for the relevant June quarter, as published
      `dependent children aged 0 to 12` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your relevant dependent children are aged 0 to 12
      `dependent children aged 13 or over` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your relevant dependent children are aged 13 or over
      `my percentage of care for them` IS A NUMBER @desc Your percentage of care for those children (100 if they live with you full-time)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my relevant dependent child amount` IS
    `the number of them` TIMES
        `rounded to the nearest dollar`
            (`What is my cost percentage` `my percentage of care for them` DIVIDED BY 100
                TIMES `What are the costs of the child` `step 1` `the annualised MTAWE figure` `dependent children aged 0 to 12` `dependent children aged 13 or over`)
    WHERE
        `the number of them` MEANS `dependent children aged 0 to 12` PLUS `dependent children aged 13 or over`
        `step 1` MEANS `the greater of` 0 (`my adjusted taxable income` MINUS `What is my self-support amount` `the annualised MTAWE figure`)

-- s 41(2) formula, with (5).
@export What is my child support income, if I have relevant dependent children (s 41(2), (5))?
GIVEN `my adjusted taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your adjusted taxable income (s 43)
      `the annualised MTAWE figure` IS A NUMBER @desc The annualised MTAWE figure for the relevant June quarter, as published
      `dependent children aged 0 to 12` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your relevant dependent children are aged 0 to 12
      `dependent children aged 13 or over` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your relevant dependent children are aged 13 or over
      `my percentage of care for them` IS A NUMBER @desc Your percentage of care for those children
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my child support income with relevant dependent children` IS
    `rounded to the nearest dollar`
        (`the greater of` 0
            ((`my adjusted taxable income` MINUS `What is my self-support amount` `the annualised MTAWE figure`)
             MINUS `What is my relevant dependent child amount` `my adjusted taxable income` `the annualised MTAWE figure`
                       `dependent children aged 0 to 12` `dependent children aged 13 or over` `my percentage of care for them`))

§§ `ss 35, 41(2), 55B-55D, 65A, 66 -- how much must I pay, with relevant dependent children`

DECLARE `Relevant dependent children` HAS
    `my dependent children aged 0 to 12`                IS A NUMBER
    `my dependent children aged 13 or over`             IS A NUMBER
    `my percentage of care for them`                    IS A NUMBER
    `the other parent's dependent children aged 0 to 12` IS A NUMBER
    `the other parent's dependent children aged 13 or over` IS A NUMBER
    `the other parent's percentage of care for them`    IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the case` IS A `My child support case`, `d` IS A `Relevant dependent children`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `my income after dependants in` `the case` `d` IS
    `What is my child support income with relevant dependent children` (`the case`'s `my adjusted taxable income`) (`the case`'s `the annualised MTAWE figure`)
        (`d`'s `my dependent children aged 0 to 12`) (`d`'s `my dependent children aged 13 or over`) (`d`'s `my percentage of care for them`)

GIVEN `the case` IS A `My child support case`, `d` IS A `Relevant dependent children`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the other parent's income after dependants in` `the case` `d` IS
    `What is my child support income with relevant dependent children` (`the case`'s `the other parent's adjusted taxable income`) (`the case`'s `the annualised MTAWE figure`)
        (`d`'s `the other parent's dependent children aged 0 to 12`) (`d`'s `the other parent's dependent children aged 13 or over`) (`d`'s `the other parent's percentage of care for them`)

-- s 55B, rounded as csa-formula.l4 rounds it.
@export What is my income percentage, with relevant dependent children (ss 41(2), 55B)?
GIVEN `the case` IS A `My child support case` @desc Your child support case
      `d` IS A `Relevant dependent children` @desc Each parent's relevant dependent children and care of them
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my income percentage with dependants` IS
    IF `combined` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
    ELSE `rounded to 2 decimal places` (`my income after dependants in` `the case` `d` TIMES 100 DIVIDED BY `combined`)
    WHERE
        `combined` MEANS `my income after dependants in` `the case` `d` PLUS `the other parent's income after dependants in` `the case` `d`

@export What is my child support percentage, with relevant dependent children (s 55D)?
GIVEN `the case` IS A `My child support case` @desc Your child support case
      `d` IS A `Relevant dependent children` @desc Each parent's relevant dependent children and care of them
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my child support percentage with dependants` IS
    `the greater of` 0 (`What is my income percentage with dependants` `the case` `d` MINUS `What is my cost percentage` (`my care in` `the case`))

-- s 35 step 8 per child, rounded (s 156), times the number of children; the costs of the child on the combined income after
-- the relevant dependent child amounts.
GIVEN `the case` IS A `My child support case`, `d` IS A `Relevant dependent children`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the formula rate with dependants in` `the case` `d` IS
    `the number of children in` `the case` TIMES
        `rounded to the nearest dollar`
            (`What is my child support percentage with dependants` `the case` `d` DIVIDED BY 100
                TIMES `What are the costs of the child`
                        (`my income after dependants in` `the case` `d` PLUS `the other parent's income after dependants in` `the case` `d`)
                        (`the case`'s `the annualised MTAWE figure`) (`the case`'s `children aged 0 to 12`) (`the case`'s `children aged 13 or over`))

-- The same order as csa-formula.l4's `How much child support must I pay`: an agreement or departure; s 65A (which turns on
-- adjusted taxable income, so is unchanged); s 66 against the rate now worked out; s 40C; s 40D; the formula.
@export How much child support must I pay a year, if either parent has relevant dependent children (ss 35, 41(2), 46, 40C, 40D, 65A, 66)?
GIVEN `the case` IS A `My child support case` @desc Your child support case, as for the question without relevant dependent children
      `d` IS A `Relevant dependent children` @desc Each parent's relevant dependent children (0 if none) and percentage of care of them
GIVETH A `My assessment`
DECIDE `How much child support must I pay with relevant dependent children` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the case`'s `a departure determination, departure order or child support agreement sets the rate`
            THEN `My assessment` WITH `how it is worked out` IS `outside this encoding: a departure determination, departure order or child support agreement sets the rate (s 35C)`
                                      `my annual rate for all the children` IS 0
        IF `I am assessed as a low income parent in` `the case`
            THEN `My assessment` WITH `how it is worked out` IS `as a low income parent not on income support (s 65A)`
                                      `my annual rate for all the children` IS `the case`'s `the low income annual rate` TIMES (`the lesser of` (`the number of children in` `the case`) 3)
        IF     (NOT `has at least regular care` (`my care in` `the case`))
           AND `the number of children in` `the case` GREATER THAN 0
           AND `the Part 5 rate` LESS THAN `the case`'s `the minimum annual rate of child support`
            THEN `My assessment` WITH `how it is worked out` IS `at the minimum annual rate (s 66)`
                                      `my annual rate for all the children` IS `the case`'s `the minimum annual rate of child support`
        IF `the other parent's care in` `the case` LESS THAN 35
            THEN `My assessment` WITH `how it is worked out` IS `nil because the other parent has less than 35% care (s 40C)`
                                      `my annual rate for all the children` IS 0
        IF `What is my child support percentage with dependants` `the case` `d` EQUALS 0
            THEN `My assessment` WITH `how it is worked out` IS `nil because my child support percentage is nil (s 40D)`
                                      `my annual rate for all the children` IS 0
        OTHERWISE `My assessment` WITH `how it is worked out` IS `by the formula (s 35)`
                                       `my annual rate for all the children` IS `the formula rate with dependants in` `the case` `d`
    WHERE
        `the Part 5 rate` MEANS
            IF `the other parent's care in` `the case` LESS THAN 35 THEN 0 ELSE `the formula rate with dependants in` `the case` `d`

§§ `ss 58(3), (4), 58AA -- adjusted taxable income from an older tax year`

-- s 58AA(1) formula and (2): to 3 decimal places, rounding up if the fourth is 5 or more. The AWE amounts are inputs.
@export What is the ATI indexation factor (s 58AA)?
GIVEN `AWE amount for the December quarter of the last relevant year of income` IS A NUMBER @desc Average Weekly Earnings (trend, persons, all employees total earnings) for that December quarter
      `AWE amount for the December quarter of the tax return year` IS A NUMBER @desc The same figure for the December quarter of the year whose tax assessment is used
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the ATI indexation factor` IS
    `rounded to 3 places` (`AWE amount for the December quarter of the last relevant year of income` DIVIDED BY `AWE amount for the December quarter of the tax return year`)
    WHERE
        `rounded to 3 places` MEANS GIVEN x YIELD FLOOR ((x TIMES 1000) PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 1000

-- s 58(3): where the year before the last relevant year of income has been assessed, the Registrar "may determine" the ATI for
-- the last relevant year as the earlier year's ATI x the ATI indexation factor. (4): where only an earlier year has been
-- assessed, "the greater of" that year's ATI x the factor and "two-thirds of the annualised MTAWE figure". Rounded to the
-- dollar (s 156).
@export If the Registrar uses an older tax assessment, what adjusted taxable income may be determined for me (s 58(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my adjusted taxable income for the assessed year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your adjusted taxable income for the most recent year whose tax has been assessed
      `the assessed year is the year before the last relevant year of income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that is the year just before the last relevant year of income (s 58(3)); otherwise an earlier year (s 58(4))
      `the ATI indexation factor` IS A NUMBER @desc The ATI indexation factor under s 58AA
      `the annualised MTAWE figure` IS A NUMBER @desc The annualised MTAWE figure for the relevant June quarter
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What adjusted taxable income may be determined for me` IS
    IF `the assessed year is the year before the last relevant year of income`
    THEN `rounded to the nearest dollar` `indexed`
    ELSE `rounded to the nearest dollar` (`the greater of` `indexed` (`the annualised MTAWE figure` TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 3))
    WHERE
        `indexed` MEANS `my adjusted taxable income for the assessed year` TIMES `the ATI indexation factor`
